  "scenario": {
    "summary": "On the compare page, verifies each of the four compared products' details (name, price, brand, descriptions, specification, shipping, min/max quantity) under their labels.",
    "steps": [
      "Verify the compare container",
      "For each product: verify the labels and values of its column"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "product"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "None"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Each product's attribute values equal the sheet values"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "dependsOn navigateToProductComparePage. First method captures: addProductsToCompareList is the head (verifyMaximumLimitReachedMessagePopup and navigateToProductComparePage depend on it; verifyProductDetails, verifySendEmailFunctionality and verifyBackLinkFunctionality depend on navigateToProductComparePage). It declares product1..product5 and compare; later methods read the class fields.",
      "ProductName values are product1..product4.name (class fields). The literals DeWalt/Bosch/OrbitSander/AngleGrinder are sheet column keys: config. Labels (Product Name, Price, Brand, ...) are UI texts: expected-output.",
      "Not scanned: the attribute values come from the productCompare sheet inside verifyCompareProductSpecificDetails; the migrated method compares productN.brandName, retailPrice, shortDescription, details, specifications, shippingInfo, minQuantity, maxQuantity (class fields).",
      "HEAD RECORD VALUES (first method captures): productDetailsData/ProductName/DeWalt -> product1.name; productDetailsData/ProductName/Bosch -> product2.name; productDetailsData/ProductName/OrbitSander -> product3.name; productDetailsData/ProductName/AngleGrinder -> product4.name. These values belong to a record the head method declares (as data with that output there); this method has no needs, so they are recorded as expected-output copies (chain rule confirmed by the user 2026-11-10). The migrated method reads them from the class field (alias.output above), not from the sheet; after migration and rescan they leave this entry.",
      "Store: openWebstoreUrl opens automation_webStoreUrl (atstage: webstore-z10-atstage, the main store MaxwellsHardware), the same store as the Selenium pdp/quickOrder entries.",
      "Profile: work/profiles/profile.json has no observations for these Selenium cells (profiled false); DB facts from bin/tda rows (2026-11-10) where cited.",
      "Scanned constant values (locators, report messages, map key prefixes, regex) are framework constants: role config, no need.",
      "migrate: Selenium reads Excel tables through TestData.getMap / getHashMap; there is no swap for Selenium."
    ],
    "confidence": "medium",
    "needsReview": true
  },
